        <body>
            <div xml:id="d370">

                <pb facs="0614" n="502" xml:id="pg502"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 5727/141.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Italian
                        Chargé</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1907-10-17"><hi rendition="#italic">October 17,
                        1907</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 543.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge receipt of
                    your note of the 4th instant, relative to acceptance by the appraising officers
                    of the United States of the certificates of value issued by Italian chambers of
                    commerce.</p>
                <p>In reply I have the honor to inform you that this question has been referred to
                    the Secretary of the Treasury, whose decision will be communicated promptly to
                    you.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Alvey A. Adee.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
